WEBVTT

00:02.069 --> 00:03.352
<i>Previously on</i> Lost:

00:03.404 --> 00:05.114
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

00:05.155 --> 00:08.857
Yes, yes, I can hear you.
Are you on the boat?

00:08.909 --> 00:10.786
- <i>What boat?</i>
- Your boat.

00:10.828 --> 00:12.861
<i>I'm not on a boat.</i>

00:12.913 --> 00:16.365
- Naomi parachuted.
- <i>Who's Naomi?</i>

00:16.417 --> 00:17.699
I've got it! I've got a signal!

00:17.751 --> 00:21.370
It's gonna work. It's happening.
We're getting off this island.

00:25.509 --> 00:27.709
<i>Hello? Is Desmond there?</i>

00:28.470 --> 00:29.544
Penny!

00:30.055 --> 00:31.338
No!

00:33.892 --> 00:37.511
I'm telling you, making that call
is the beginning of the end.

00:37.563 --> 00:40.232
- Who is this?
- <i>Who is this?</i>

00:42.109 --> 00:45.560
I'm one of the survivors
of Oceanic flight 815.

00:46.989 --> 00:50.159
- Can you get a fix on our location?
- <i>Sit tight.</i>

00:50.200 --> 00:52.025
<i>We'll be right there.</i>

01:20.856 --> 01:25.434
<i>...almost 30 minutes now since the start</i>
<i>of this high-speed chase.</i>

01:25.486 --> 01:28.739
<i>Still have no information</i>
<i>about who's driving this vehicle.</i>

01:29.156 --> 01:31.773
<i>Jeff</i>, <i>can you tell us</i>
<i>where the chase started?</i>

01:31.825 --> 01:35.402
<i>We're hearing reports that the pursuit</i>
<i>began near the La Brea area</i>,

01:35.454 --> 01:39.156
<i>then travelled through a warehouse</i>
<i>district south of the 10 freeway.</i>

01:39.208 --> 01:41.616
<i>Can you see how many people</i>
<i>are in the car?</i>

01:41.669 --> 01:44.161
<i>It appears to be just the one</i>,
<i>the driver.</i>

01:44.213 --> 01:46.580
<i>We're not sure if that's</i>
<i>the owner of the car.</i>

01:46.632 --> 01:49.468
<i>What you're seeing here</i>
<i>are pictures of the 10 freeway</i>

01:49.510 --> 01:52.377
- <i>south of downtown.</i>
- <i>Is that a Camaro</i>, <i>Jeff?</i>

01:52.429 --> 01:56.006
<i>Yes</i>, <i>it looks like a vintage</i>
<i>early '70s model.</i>

01:56.058 --> 01:57.132
Damn it.

02:17.579 --> 02:19.321
Show us your hands!

02:26.005 --> 02:29.122
Roll down the window
and show us your hands now!

02:39.226 --> 02:41.468
Slowly open the door
with your left hand.

02:49.111 --> 02:50.227
Get out of the car!

02:51.655 --> 02:53.532
Turn around, slow.

03:08.339 --> 03:09.715
On the ground!

03:10.966 --> 03:12.040
Now!

03:18.682 --> 03:20.340
Stop! Don't you know who I am?

03:20.392 --> 03:24.521
Stop, wait! Don't you know who I am?
I'm one of the Oceanic Six!

03:25.731 --> 03:27.524
I'm one of the Oceanic Six!

03:43.999 --> 03:46.919
So five minutes
before you led ten cruisers

03:46.961 --> 03:48.785
on a chase across the city,

03:48.837 --> 03:52.091
you're minding your own business
in a convenience store?

03:52.716 --> 03:56.209
Until you see something and freak out.

03:57.054 --> 03:59.421
Mr Reyes, why did you run like that?

03:59.473 --> 04:02.007
Who'd you see in there?

04:03.018 --> 04:05.854
Listen, buddy, I know you saw
somebody in that store

04:05.896 --> 04:09.181
- that made you run away...
- Wasn't running away from anyone.

04:09.233 --> 04:12.069
Do you think I care
that you're a celebrity?

04:12.111 --> 04:15.114
You crashed your Camaro
in the wrong neighbourhood.

04:15.155 --> 04:16.313
I'm not a celebrity.

04:18.325 --> 04:21.610
Is that why you kept shouting,
"I'm one of the Oceanic Six"?

04:22.955 --> 04:25.489
You want to know a funny coincidence?

04:26.041 --> 04:27.115
Sure.

04:28.335 --> 04:30.243
I knew somebody on your plane.

04:31.380 --> 04:33.090
Really?

04:34.425 --> 04:36.666
Her name was Ana Lucia Cortez.

04:37.344 --> 04:40.514
She was my partner
before I made detective.

04:40.556 --> 04:43.340
Dark hair.

04:43.392 --> 04:45.425
Gorgeous.

04:47.813 --> 04:49.690
Maybe you knew her.

04:52.151 --> 04:56.103
Maybe met her on the plane,
before it took off?

04:58.073 --> 04:59.731
Sorry, never met her.

05:05.831 --> 05:08.532
Why don't you watch the tape?

05:09.084 --> 05:11.076
Maybe it'll spark something.

05:12.421 --> 05:14.131
I'm gonna get a doughnut.

05:14.173 --> 05:15.633
You want one?

05:16.508 --> 05:18.834
- No, thanks.
- When I come back,

05:18.886 --> 05:21.253
you're gonna tell me who you ran from.

05:52.211 --> 05:53.702
Hey!

05:53.754 --> 05:55.037
Help!

05:57.091 --> 05:58.634
Help!

05:58.676 --> 06:01.084
Help! Help me, help!

06:01.512 --> 06:03.920
What the hell is wrong with you?

06:03.973 --> 06:06.506
What are you doing, Reyes?

06:06.558 --> 06:08.884
You trying to get tossed
into the nuthouse?

06:08.936 --> 06:12.471
Because if that's what you want
I can make that happen right now.

06:12.523 --> 06:13.983
You can?

06:14.483 --> 06:16.110
Oh, thank you.

06:16.151 --> 06:18.935
Thank you, thank you.

06:21.031 --> 06:24.691
Jack, you there, dude?
Beach to Jack. Come in, Jack.

06:25.703 --> 06:28.372
- <i>Beach to Jack.</i>
- Right here, Hurley. What's up?

06:28.414 --> 06:31.948
Hey, did you guys make it
to that radio tower thingy yet?

06:32.001 --> 06:34.534
Yeah. And I talked to the people
on the boat.

06:34.586 --> 06:36.912
They're on their way
to pick us up right now.

06:36.964 --> 06:39.247
Seriously? It worked?

06:39.300 --> 06:42.501
Seriously. We're all on the way
back to the beach right now,

06:42.553 --> 06:44.836
so you better pack your bags, buddy.

06:46.724 --> 06:48.548
<i>Dude</i>, <i>that's great!</i>

06:56.066 --> 06:58.684
- Any luck?
- Nothing, no sign of him.

06:58.736 --> 07:00.696
It's like he just disappeared.

07:01.947 --> 07:03.741
Why would Locke kill her?

07:03.782 --> 07:06.024
- He hadn't met her.
- Because he's crazy.

07:06.076 --> 07:07.953
So, what if he comes back?

07:07.995 --> 07:10.570
He comes back, I'm gonna kill him.

07:16.503 --> 07:18.380
I'm gonna get everybody together.

07:18.422 --> 07:20.747
Sooner we get back
to the beach the better.

07:24.053 --> 07:25.596
Are we really going home?

07:27.890 --> 07:29.631
Yeah, we're really going home.

07:38.692 --> 07:42.738
I can't believe I'm actually going
to have my baby in a hospital.

07:42.780 --> 07:44.573
Oh, rub it in, why don't you?

07:44.615 --> 07:47.399
- Oh, no...
- You ladies need a hand?

07:47.451 --> 07:49.943
No, we're just
wrapping things up, thanks.

07:51.121 --> 07:55.751
You must be very proud of Bernard.
I hear he's quite the hero.

07:55.793 --> 07:58.963
Everyone up here knows
the real hero is your man, Claire.

07:59.004 --> 08:01.674
If Charlie didn't turn off that gizmo

08:01.715 --> 08:05.052
we'd still be getting a busy signal
on that fancy phone.

08:06.470 --> 08:10.933
So you better make sure you treat him
real good when we get back.

08:10.975 --> 08:13.008
Rose!

08:16.188 --> 08:17.815
OK, thanks, I have enough.

08:17.856 --> 08:20.432
I need you to do me a favour.

08:22.486 --> 08:26.438
I need you to take Alex and
get as far from here as possible.

08:26.490 --> 08:27.647
What?

08:27.700 --> 08:29.691
Listen, we don't have time for this.

08:29.743 --> 08:32.997
Everyone who stays here is going to die.

08:33.038 --> 08:35.906
Now get Alex and get away right now.

08:35.958 --> 08:38.325
I don't care where you go, just go.

08:38.377 --> 08:40.994
I will not have my daughter...

08:43.424 --> 08:45.874
She's not your daughter.

09:03.986 --> 09:06.228
Did I ever tell you I won the lottery?

09:08.324 --> 09:13.110
I got, like, $150 million.
Worst thing that ever happened to me.

09:13.162 --> 09:15.654
Oh, yeah, who needs $150 million?

09:15.706 --> 09:19.533
Now it'll all be gone
'cause they all think I'm dead.

09:20.336 --> 09:23.370
When we get rescued and I go back...

09:24.632 --> 09:26.258
...l'm gonna be free.

09:31.513 --> 09:33.004
I want to do a cannonball.

09:34.433 --> 09:38.093
I've been walking up and down
this beach every day

09:38.145 --> 09:41.722
and looking out at this water,
and I want to do a cannonball.

09:43.150 --> 09:46.153
Hurley, you want to do a cannonball?

09:46.779 --> 09:48.020
Cannonball.

10:34.493 --> 10:37.778
We need to get to Jack. We can't
let him get in touch with that boat.

10:37.830 --> 10:40.864
Easy, Scotty, everything's cool.
The boat's on the way.

10:40.916 --> 10:42.626
What? On the way? No.

10:42.668 --> 10:44.868
- Where's Charlie?
- That woman Naomi lied.

10:44.920 --> 10:47.454
The people on the boat
aren't who they say they are!

10:47.506 --> 10:49.581
- Then who are they?
- Where's Charlie?

10:49.633 --> 10:52.125
I don't know, but we need
to get in touch with Jack now!

10:52.177 --> 10:54.586
- We can call him, we have a walkie.
- Get it!

10:54.638 --> 10:57.725
- What do you mean people aren't who...?
- Where's Charlie?!

11:04.106 --> 11:07.057
I'm... I'm sorry, brother. I...

11:31.884 --> 11:33.344
That's our ride.

11:35.304 --> 11:36.795
- Hello?
- <i>Hey</i>, <i>Jack.</i>

11:36.847 --> 11:40.340
<i>This is George Minkowski. We're</i>
<i>trying to get a lock on your signal</i>,

11:40.392 --> 11:42.509
<i>but we're getting some RF interference.</i>

11:42.561 --> 11:45.898
<i>We're gonna need to rejigger</i>
<i>some settings on your sat-phone.</i>

11:45.940 --> 11:47.931
Sure. OK, just tell me what I gotta do.

11:47.983 --> 11:50.017
<i>How about you put Naomi on?</i>

11:50.903 --> 11:53.311
Naomi went to get some firewood.

11:53.364 --> 11:56.200
Can you hold on for a second?
Let me see if I can...

12:10.130 --> 12:11.455
Where is she?

12:21.308 --> 12:22.632
We gotta call the doc.

12:23.269 --> 12:26.136
Did you listen to Desmond?
Charlie wrote on his hand...

12:26.188 --> 12:28.221
Look, I'm sorry he's dead.

12:28.274 --> 12:30.724
I don't even know what
"not Penny's boat" means.

12:30.776 --> 12:33.862
- Calling Jack accomplishes nothing.
- It would warn him.

12:33.904 --> 12:37.439
It also warns the people on
the freighter we're suspicious of them.

12:37.491 --> 12:40.577
They're monitoring our communications.
If we call Jack...

12:40.619 --> 12:42.778
I got the walkie, I'm making the call.

12:49.211 --> 12:51.244
We better get going.

12:55.968 --> 12:57.344
Going where?

13:03.475 --> 13:05.801
I found blood. The girl's trail.

13:05.853 --> 13:07.177
Probably crawled away.

13:07.229 --> 13:11.275
Can't be more than ten minutes ahead
of us. We should go, now, and find her.

13:11.650 --> 13:15.018
- We're taking him with us.
- And why would we do that?

13:15.070 --> 13:17.740
Because I don't trust him
with anybody but me.

13:21.035 --> 13:22.317
All right, listen up.

13:22.369 --> 13:24.736
I need all of you
to head back to the beach.

13:24.788 --> 13:26.196
When these people show up,

13:26.248 --> 13:29.533
we want to make sure
we're real easy for them to find, OK?

13:29.585 --> 13:31.868
- Yeah.
- You look worried, Jack.

13:34.340 --> 13:37.457
The only thing I'm worried about
is missing our ride home.

13:42.723 --> 13:45.893
I found her trail. She's headed west
across the island.

13:46.727 --> 13:49.761
Rousseau already found it.
We're going after her now.

13:50.981 --> 13:53.932
But... Are you sure it's hers?

13:53.984 --> 13:56.059
Unless someone else is bleeding.

13:56.111 --> 13:59.896
If she didn't want us to find her,
she could've created a dummy trail.

13:59.949 --> 14:02.232
- I think we should follow both...
- Kate.

14:02.284 --> 14:05.152
Six hours from now,
we're gonna be sitting on that boat,

14:05.204 --> 14:09.416
laughing about the fact there was
one final thing we couldn't agree upon.

14:09.959 --> 14:12.117
Naomi is hurt. She ran into the jungle.

14:12.169 --> 14:14.703
She's not thinking about
leaving fake trails.

14:16.257 --> 14:18.457
- You're right.
- I'll track her down.

14:18.509 --> 14:20.876
Why don't you get everybody
back to the beach?

14:20.928 --> 14:22.044
You got it.

14:30.980 --> 14:32.387
Be careful, OK?

14:33.023 --> 14:34.097
Yeah.

14:45.953 --> 14:49.780
What the hell's gotten into you, Hugo?
They'll all be back in the morning.

14:49.832 --> 14:52.240
- We just wait.
- You don't wait with warnings.

14:52.293 --> 14:53.450
You warn.

15:06.056 --> 15:08.976
Here I was thinking I was gonna get
a good night's sleep.

15:19.111 --> 15:20.686
You almost got me that time.

15:20.738 --> 15:23.689
How about best out of seven?

15:24.658 --> 15:26.817
Are you ready for your meds, Hugo?

15:28.454 --> 15:30.696
By the way, you have a visitor.

15:41.675 --> 15:43.052
Mr Reyes.

15:43.969 --> 15:45.210
Hello.

15:45.262 --> 15:49.475
My name is Matthew Abbadon.
I'm an attorney for Oceanic Airlines.

15:51.101 --> 15:52.895
Can we talk for a few minutes?

15:55.397 --> 15:56.774
OK.

16:01.278 --> 16:06.398
I'm here, Mr Reyes, 'cause we heard
about your recent... episode.

16:07.034 --> 16:10.120
Your arrest, your incarceration here.

16:11.288 --> 16:13.780
Frankly, we feel terrible about it.

16:15.042 --> 16:17.451
So, on behalf of Oceanic,

16:17.503 --> 16:20.620
I'd like to extend you an invitation
for a little upgrade.

16:22.049 --> 16:24.374
What kind of upgrade?

16:26.345 --> 16:29.546
To a facility where the paint
isn't peeling off the walls.

16:30.432 --> 16:33.769
Where you'd have your own bathroom.
You can see the ocean...

16:33.811 --> 16:35.635
I don't want to see the ocean.

16:37.564 --> 16:38.764
No problem.

16:41.694 --> 16:45.562
Actually, thanks. I'm fine right here.

16:47.199 --> 16:49.775
Are you fine, Mr Reyes?

16:50.911 --> 16:52.069
What do you mean?

16:52.746 --> 16:54.456
You're in a mental institution.

16:56.458 --> 16:58.450
Who'd you say you were again?

16:59.461 --> 17:01.995
I'd like to see a business card.

17:07.011 --> 17:09.044
I must have left them at home.

17:11.307 --> 17:13.100
Then we're done, dude.

17:14.435 --> 17:16.343
Are they still alive?

17:19.815 --> 17:21.191
What?

17:22.401 --> 17:23.600
You heard me.

17:24.612 --> 17:26.812
Nurse! Nurse!

17:26.864 --> 17:29.064
Get out of here!
You better get out of here!

17:29.116 --> 17:31.400
Help me! He's after me!
No, no, no!

17:31.452 --> 17:33.735
- That guy's after me. Help me.
- OK, OK.

17:52.389 --> 17:54.099
All right there, Hugo?

17:54.141 --> 17:55.935
Yeah, dude, I'm fine.

17:57.519 --> 18:00.012
- You want to talk about it?
- Talk about what?

18:00.064 --> 18:01.555
Charlie.

18:06.946 --> 18:10.897
I mean, you two were buddies.
I just thought...

18:12.284 --> 18:15.318
We'll probably get to Jack faster
if we don't talk.

18:22.544 --> 18:25.037
I'm gonna head up
and tell them to slow down.

18:25.089 --> 18:27.456
- I can keep up.
- All right, <i>ese.</i>

18:27.508 --> 18:30.959
Just... holler if you need me.

19:02.876 --> 19:04.253
Guys!

19:04.878 --> 19:06.255
Guys!

19:07.423 --> 19:08.830
Guys!

19:13.554 --> 19:14.836
Guys!

19:20.477 --> 19:21.854
Guys!

19:37.411 --> 19:39.288
Uh-oh.

19:47.129 --> 19:48.537
The blood trail ends here.

19:49.465 --> 19:50.539
What do you mean?

19:51.717 --> 19:52.791
It ends.

19:52.843 --> 19:55.377
Are you telling me
she stopped bleeding here?

19:55.429 --> 19:58.766
No. I'm telling you she fooled us
and doubled back.

19:59.433 --> 20:00.716
Better call the boat,

20:00.768 --> 20:03.969
tell them she's getting
a really big bundle of firewood.

20:12.696 --> 20:13.854
Where is it?

20:13.906 --> 20:16.690
I probably should've told you
I saw her take the phone,

20:16.742 --> 20:18.619
but you'd beat me up, Jack.

20:19.578 --> 20:21.862
- I owed you one.
- What are you talking about?

20:21.914 --> 20:24.197
Kate took it when she hugged you.

20:27.169 --> 20:30.089
She found the right trail.
You wouldn't listen to her.

20:30.130 --> 20:32.664
I guess she's taken matters
into her own hands.

20:32.716 --> 20:36.543
Look on the bright side, somebody
around here knows what they're doing.

21:16.844 --> 21:18.960
- Hello?
- <i>Who's this?</i>

21:20.931 --> 21:23.256
- This is Kate.
- <i>You with Jack?</i>

21:23.309 --> 21:26.510
- No, he's not here.
- <i>Where's Naomi?</i>

21:28.689 --> 21:30.180
We're looking for her.

21:30.232 --> 21:32.557
<i>What do you mean</i>,
<i>you're looking for her?</i>

21:45.039 --> 21:46.238
Give me the phone.

21:48.626 --> 21:51.378
- Give me the phone.
- Naomi, listen to me.

21:51.420 --> 21:54.371
- You're hurt, let me help you.
- Help me?

21:54.423 --> 21:58.500
I just spent the last three days
trying to get you people rescued,

21:58.552 --> 22:00.585
and you throw this knife in my back.

22:00.638 --> 22:02.598
No, no. That was not us.

22:03.432 --> 22:05.340
- Who?
- His name is John Locke.

22:06.352 --> 22:08.635
- Why?
- He said you weren't who you said.

22:11.065 --> 22:14.266
I swear to God we would
never hurt you. You know us.

22:15.027 --> 22:17.477
Please. We need your help.
Please help us.

22:17.529 --> 22:19.563
Give me the phone.

22:25.412 --> 22:27.863
George, it's Naomi.

22:27.915 --> 22:31.491
<i>Naomi</i>, <i>where have you been?</i>
<i>What's going on over there?</i>

22:34.171 --> 22:37.622
I had an accident. I'm hurt.

22:37.675 --> 22:41.293
<i>An accident? What accident?</i>
<i>What happened?</i>

22:42.471 --> 22:43.962
<i>Naomi.</i>

22:44.848 --> 22:45.922
<i>Hello?</i>

22:46.392 --> 22:49.092
- <i>Hello.</i>
- I hit a tree branch...

22:49.853 --> 22:51.563
...when I parachuted in.

22:52.106 --> 22:53.482
Took it through my gut.

22:53.524 --> 22:55.932
<i>Why did they tell me</i>
<i>you were getting firewood?</i>

22:55.985 --> 22:59.728
I guess they were afraid to tell you
what happened till I could talk to you.

22:59.780 --> 23:02.814
<i>We've lost our signal</i>,
<i>and we can't come get you.</i>

23:02.866 --> 23:05.067
<i>Can you change</i>
<i>your tracking frequency?</i>

23:05.119 --> 23:06.662
Yeah.

23:10.332 --> 23:11.875
Try it now.

23:12.501 --> 23:13.961
<i>Clear as a bell.</i>

23:14.003 --> 23:17.871
<i>Hang on</i>, <i>Naomi</i>, <i>we'll get you</i>
<i>back here ASAP</i>, <i>OK?</i>

23:17.923 --> 23:20.165
I'm sorry, George.

23:22.261 --> 23:24.753
Just tell my sister that I love her.

23:34.231 --> 23:35.472
Hello?

24:19.860 --> 24:21.101
Help!

24:21.779 --> 24:23.656
Help!

24:23.697 --> 24:25.074
Help!

24:40.381 --> 24:42.039
There's nothing here.

24:42.091 --> 24:43.550
There's nothing here.

24:43.592 --> 24:45.302
There's nothing here.

24:45.344 --> 24:47.085
There's nothing here!

25:00.109 --> 25:01.600
Hello, Hugo.

25:04.071 --> 25:06.646
You've got yourself
good and lost out here, Hugo.

25:09.118 --> 25:11.651
How did you get separated
from the group?

25:15.416 --> 25:16.573
I just...

25:18.419 --> 25:19.962
...fell behind, I guess.

25:20.004 --> 25:22.756
Is that why you were shouting for help?

25:22.798 --> 25:24.508
I got scared.

25:28.345 --> 25:31.348
What Desmond said happened
down in that station,

25:32.099 --> 25:34.341
"Not Penny's boat."

25:34.893 --> 25:37.646
Are you sure that's what
Charlie wrote on his hand?

25:38.188 --> 25:40.472
Jack should never have called
those people.

25:40.524 --> 25:42.432
I couldn't agree more.

25:44.236 --> 25:47.354
It's gonna be hard
to talk him into thinking

25:47.406 --> 25:49.366
they're not coming here to rescue us.

25:49.408 --> 25:52.609
Well, guess we're gonna have
to try our best, Hugo...

25:53.704 --> 25:56.540
...because if we can't talk him
out of it...

25:58.459 --> 26:00.367
...then Charlie died for nothing.

26:16.644 --> 26:18.520
Where the hell have you been,
Hugo?

26:18.562 --> 26:22.691
Sorry. I was just... I got lost.

26:28.739 --> 26:30.564
What are you doing here?

26:31.951 --> 26:34.192
I came here
for the same reason you did,

26:34.244 --> 26:36.570
to warn Jack about the people
on that boat.

26:36.622 --> 26:38.030
I already gave it a shot,

26:38.082 --> 26:41.742
but... I figured I might have
better luck with some support.

26:42.503 --> 26:43.994
You want my support?

26:44.046 --> 26:46.913
You can tell me why you destroyed
that submarine.

27:24.128 --> 27:25.921
Still in one piece.

27:25.963 --> 27:27.204
Rambo.

27:40.894 --> 27:42.354
I'll tell her.

28:06.795 --> 28:08.339
He's dead.

28:11.842 --> 28:13.875
Charlie's dead.

28:15.012 --> 28:16.211
No.

28:39.620 --> 28:41.653
I'd watch out if I were you.

28:42.289 --> 28:44.166
What are you talking about, dude?

28:44.208 --> 28:47.461
There's a guy over there,
staring at you.

28:48.212 --> 28:50.579
- What guy?
- That guy.

28:53.968 --> 28:55.208
Hey, man.

28:56.095 --> 28:57.377
Don't run.

28:58.931 --> 29:02.017
Hurley, just...

29:02.059 --> 29:03.633
Just...

29:04.311 --> 29:05.552
Sit down.

29:06.855 --> 29:08.263
I want to talk to you.

29:11.318 --> 29:12.778
Come on.

29:13.570 --> 29:15.854
Don't do what you did in the store, OK?

29:17.074 --> 29:20.442
There's no need to... freak out.

29:20.494 --> 29:23.862
No need to freak out? I'm trying
to buy some jerky and a Slushee,

29:23.914 --> 29:26.406
and suddenly you're
standing over by the Ho Hos.

29:26.458 --> 29:28.575
You're dead.
What do you expect me to do?

29:29.253 --> 29:31.703
Can we just... sit down?

29:32.756 --> 29:35.540
I may be in the mental hospital,
but I know you're dead,

29:35.593 --> 29:38.794
and I'm not having an imaginary
conversation with you.

29:40.014 --> 29:41.088
I am dead.

29:45.144 --> 29:46.854
But I'm also here.

29:48.314 --> 29:49.690
OK, prove it.

29:58.073 --> 30:00.357
OK, OK.

30:09.752 --> 30:12.869
Did you know you were going to die
when you swam out there?

30:22.056 --> 30:23.630
Why didn't you tell me?

30:23.682 --> 30:26.216
Because you would've tried to stop me.

30:27.478 --> 30:31.221
And since I was gonna do it anyway
I thought to spare you all the drama.

30:34.318 --> 30:36.351
And now you have to do something...

30:37.780 --> 30:39.604
...but you're hiding from it.

30:41.116 --> 30:44.818
That's the real reason you ran
when you saw me in the store.

30:44.870 --> 30:48.321
- You knew I was here to tell you.
- I'm not listening to this.

30:48.958 --> 30:50.417
No, 'cause you're not here.

30:50.459 --> 30:52.252
I am here. You're being a baby.

30:52.294 --> 30:54.661
I'm gonna close my eyes, count to five.

30:54.713 --> 30:56.997
- When I open them, you'll be gone.
- I am here.

30:57.049 --> 30:58.957
- One... two...
- Don't do this.

30:59.009 --> 31:00.636
- They need you.
- ...three...

31:00.678 --> 31:02.304
- They need you.
- ...four...

31:02.346 --> 31:04.254
- You know they need you.
- ...five!

31:20.406 --> 31:23.190
When? What happened?

31:25.995 --> 31:28.664
I mean, how did he...?

31:31.125 --> 31:33.700
He was trying to help us.

32:09.622 --> 32:10.737
Jack.

32:15.544 --> 32:17.369
You're not gonna shoot me, Jack...

32:18.505 --> 32:20.747
...any more than I was gonna shoot...

32:24.929 --> 32:26.586
It's not loaded.

32:33.604 --> 32:36.096
- Come on, Jack.
- Let go of me!

32:39.401 --> 32:41.893
- Do you know what he did?
- Yes, I know what he did!

32:41.946 --> 32:43.489
All I did...

32:44.657 --> 32:47.190
All I have ever done...

32:47.743 --> 32:50.027
...has been in the best interest
of all of us.

32:50.079 --> 32:51.653
Are you insane?

32:56.168 --> 32:58.744
I know,
I have a lot of explaining to do,

32:58.796 --> 33:03.175
but I never did anything
to hurt any of you.

33:03.217 --> 33:06.668
I even risked my life to tell you
there was a traitor in your midst.

33:06.720 --> 33:07.878
She helped us, John.

33:07.930 --> 33:10.881
All you ever did was blow up
every chance we had

33:10.933 --> 33:12.810
of getting off this island.

33:12.851 --> 33:14.478
You killed Naomi!

33:14.520 --> 33:17.471
Well, technically,
he didn't kill her yet.

33:17.523 --> 33:19.348
Yes, he did.

33:22.236 --> 33:23.727
She just died.

33:24.905 --> 33:26.396
She didn't give you up, John.

33:26.448 --> 33:30.067
She covered for us, and she fixed this.

33:30.119 --> 33:31.495
They're on their way.

33:33.414 --> 33:35.238
She didn't cover for anyone.

33:35.291 --> 33:38.825
She wants her people to come here.

33:39.295 --> 33:42.496
And trust me, when they do,
we had better be far away from here.

33:44.008 --> 33:46.792
I'm going to the barracks.
The Others abandoned them.

33:46.844 --> 33:49.763
It's the only place on the island
with any form of security.

33:49.805 --> 33:52.255
It'll have to do until
I think of something else.

33:53.392 --> 33:55.884
Until then, if you want to live...

33:56.729 --> 33:58.220
...you need to come with me.

33:59.648 --> 34:02.015
No one's going anywhere
with you, John,

34:02.067 --> 34:04.737
- because they're not crazy.
- He's not crazy.

34:06.196 --> 34:07.990
What about Charlie?

34:11.076 --> 34:14.861
Charlie went down to that place
so we could all be rescued.

34:21.003 --> 34:23.954
And whatever he did down there,
it worked.

34:27.343 --> 34:29.543
But then something
must have happened...

34:31.805 --> 34:34.297
...must've heard something before he...

34:39.480 --> 34:42.889
I don't know why,
but he changed his mind.

34:50.157 --> 34:52.774
Because the last thing he did
was to warn us

34:52.826 --> 34:56.163
that the people on that boat
are not who they said they were.

35:10.970 --> 35:12.794
So I'm not listening to you.

35:16.642 --> 35:18.884
I'm listening to my friend.

35:22.606 --> 35:24.400
I'm listening to Charlie.

35:38.998 --> 35:40.280
Anyone else?

35:44.336 --> 35:45.911
There isn't much time.

36:00.686 --> 36:03.887
Jack, with your permission,
I'd like to go with John.

36:08.319 --> 36:09.893
He's all yours.

36:25.669 --> 36:27.661
You said we'd never leave the island.

36:27.713 --> 36:31.665
If you want to go with Locke,
I'll be right behind you.

36:32.468 --> 36:34.543
I'm not going anywhere with that man.

36:45.230 --> 36:46.607
What are you doing?

36:52.196 --> 36:54.813
Same thing I've always done, Kate.

36:55.950 --> 36:57.326
Surviving.

37:18.514 --> 37:21.465
You know where to find us
when you change your mind.

38:07.813 --> 38:09.096
You ever miss?

38:13.694 --> 38:14.768
Jack.

38:15.404 --> 38:19.867
Yeah. I was on my way back
from a consult.

38:19.908 --> 38:22.109
Thought I'd drop by and pay you a visit.

38:24.622 --> 38:25.946
Horse?

38:25.998 --> 38:27.458
You're on.

38:29.251 --> 38:30.909
So consult, huh?

38:30.961 --> 38:33.912
Does that mean you're back
doing surgical stuff?

38:33.964 --> 38:35.080
Yeah.

38:42.222 --> 38:43.296
H.

38:43.349 --> 38:45.142
Reporters leaving you alone?

38:48.812 --> 38:49.886
Yeah.

38:49.939 --> 38:52.973
Still have to sign some autographs
when I go out for coffee.

38:54.610 --> 38:56.351
Thinking about growing a beard.

38:59.573 --> 39:01.481
You'd look weird with a beard, dude.

39:02.910 --> 39:03.984
That's H-O.

39:05.204 --> 39:06.914
So...

39:09.291 --> 39:11.491
...what are you really doing here, Jack?

39:16.090 --> 39:19.374
I was just checking on you,
seeing if everything was OK.

39:20.552 --> 39:22.627
You're checking to see if I went nuts,

39:22.680 --> 39:24.838
if I was gonna tell.

39:26.892 --> 39:28.269
Are you?

39:33.190 --> 39:34.431
You're up.

39:37.444 --> 39:39.436
No, you win. I...

39:42.157 --> 39:43.701
I gotta run.

39:46.161 --> 39:47.871
It was great seeing you, Hurley.

39:54.461 --> 39:55.952
I'm sorry.

40:01.760 --> 40:03.919
I'm sorry I went with Locke.

40:06.807 --> 40:08.882
I should've stayed with you.

40:10.811 --> 40:12.969
It's water under the bridge, man.

40:18.986 --> 40:21.269
I don't think we did
the right thing, Jack.

40:22.615 --> 40:24.690
- I think it wants us to come back.
- Hurley.

40:24.742 --> 40:27.859
- It's gonna do everything it...
- We're never going back!

40:38.714 --> 40:40.424
Never say never, dude.

41:04.448 --> 41:06.241
Are you thinking of Charlie?

41:07.534 --> 41:10.569
Feels like a hundred years ago
we came out here together.

41:13.332 --> 41:15.125
How did this happen?

41:24.343 --> 41:26.710
Thunder's getting louder.

41:31.558 --> 41:33.216
That's not thunder.

41:33.269 --> 41:34.593
Come on.

41:45.906 --> 41:47.616
Come on.

42:13.225 --> 42:14.685
Are you Jack?
